.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm text\-block
reads text from standard input or a given file, and writes it to standard output or a given file. Various modifications can be applied according to the selected operation mode:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Cat: copy the input text as\-is.
.It
Discard: discard the input without producing output.
.It
Enumerate: prepend configurable line numbers to each line.
.It
Extract: output only the text inside marked blocks, discarding everything else.
.It
Highlight: visually highlight marked and unmarked text fragments (for example using ANSI colours and start/end symbols).
.It
Delete: remove text inside marked blocks.
.It
Insert Front: insert text from a file at the beginning of each marked block.
.It
Insert Back: insert text from a file at the end of each marked block.
.It
Replace: replace the contents of each marked block with text from a file.
.El
.Pp
Marked blocks are selected via configurable begin and end tags (for example
.Ql <BEGIN\-OF\-BLOCK>
and
.Ql <END\-OF\-BLOCK> ) .
Tag line scope is configurable:
.Bl -bullet
.It
tags\-only: only the text between the marker tags belongs to a block, allowing multiple blocks on the same line (default).
.It
full\-tag\-lines: a marker spans the entire line containing its begin or end tag. Consequently, only the
.Sy first
tag on a line is processed and any additional tags on the same line are ignored.
Hint: use Highlight mode to visualise this behaviour.
.El
.Pp
Inclusion of the marker tags themselves is also configurable:
.Bl -bullet
.It
exclude\-tags: marked text excludes the begin and end tags (default).
.It
include\-tags: marked text includes the begin and end tags.
.El
.Pp
Identical begin and end tags (for example via
.Fl t Ql <MARKER> )
define a zero\-width block at each occurrence, which is useful as an insertion anchor.
.Pp
Alternatively, blocks can be selected by a 1\-based line\-number range
.Pq Fl s Ar from\_line Ar to\_line .
Negative line numbers count backwards from the end of the file, which requires a seekable input file
.Pq Fl i Ar input\_file
rather than standard input.
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl C | Fl \-cat
Run in Cat mode (default).
.It Fl 0 | Fl \-discard
Run in Discard mode.
.It Fl H | Fl \-highlight
Run in Highlight mode.
.It Fl E | Fl \-enumerate
Run in Enumerate mode.
.It Fl X | Fl \-extract
Run in Extract mode.
.It Fl D | Fl \-delete | Fl \-remove
Run in Delete mode.
.It Fl F Ar insert\_file | Fl \-insert\-front Ar insert\_file
Run in Insert\-Front mode.
.Ql \-
reads the insertion text from standard input (requires an input file via
.Fl i ) .
.It Fl B Ar insert\_file | Fl \-insert\-back Ar insert\_file
Run in Insert\-Back mode.
.Ql \-
reads the insertion text from standard input (requires an input file via
.Fl i ) .
.It Fl R Ar insert\_file | Fl \-replace Ar insert\_file
Run in Replace mode.
.Ql \-
reads the replacement text from standard input (requires an input file via
.Fl i ) .
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints the program's command\-line parameters and exits.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints the program version and exits.
.It Fl s Ar from\_line Ar to\_line | Fl \-select Ar from\_line Ar to\_line
Select a line range from
.Ar from\_line
to
.Ar to\_line .
.Ar from\_line
= 1 starts at the first line of the file;
.Ar to\_line
= 0 extends to the end of the file.
Negative line numbers count backwards from the end of the file and require an input file
.Pq Fl i | Fl \-input .
Line selection is mutually exclusive with tag options
.Pq Fl b , Fl e , Fl t .
.It Fl b Ar begin\_tag | Fl \-begin\-tag Ar begin\_tag
Sets the begin tag. Mutually exclusive with
.Fl s | Fl \-select .
.It Fl e Ar end\_tag | Fl \-end\-tag Ar end\_tag
Sets the end tag. Mutually exclusive with
.Fl s | Fl \-select .
.It Fl t Ar tag | Fl \-tag Ar tag
Sets an identical begin and end tag. Mutually exclusive with
.Fl s | Fl \-select .
.It Fl i Ar input\_file | Fl \-input Ar input\_file
Sets the input file.
.Ql \-
reads from standard input (default).
.It Fl o Ar output\_file | Fl \-output Ar output\_file
Sets the output file (overwriting an existing file unless
.Fl a
is given).
.Ql \-
writes to standard output (default).
.It Fl a | Fl \-append
Opens the output file in append mode instead of truncating it.
.It Fl p | Fl \-in\-place
Updates the input file in place by writing to a temporary file suffixed with
.Ql ~
and atomically replacing the input file on success.
.It Fl k | Fl \-keep\-broken
Retains partial output files on error instead of deleting them (default: off).
.It Fl m Ar min\_actions | Fl \-min\-actions Ar min\_actions
Sets the minimum required number of marked\-block actions; exits with an error if fewer blocks match.
.It Fl M Ar max\_actions | Fl \-max\-actions Ar max\_actions
Sets the maximum permitted number of marked\-block actions; exits with an error if more blocks match.
.It Fl y | Fl \-include\-tags
Include the marker tags in the marked block.
.It Fl x | Fl \-exclude\-tags
Exclude the marker tags from the marked block (default).
.It Fl f | Fl \-full\-tag\-lines
Include full marker tag lines in the marked block.
.It Fl g | Fl \-tags\-only
Restrict marking to the tags themselves rather than full lines (default).
.It Fl q | Fl \-suppress\-warnings
Suppresses warnings about ineffective parameter combinations.
.It Fl \-enumerate\-format Ar format
In Enumerate mode, sets the
.Xr printf 3
flag and field\-width specification for line numbers (without a leading
.Ql %
or conversion specifier). Examples:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Ql 06
\(-> 6\-digit zero\-padded numbers such as
.Ql 000001
(default).
.It
.Ql 4
\(-> 4\-digit space\-padded numbers such as
.Ql "   2" .
.It
.Ql \-4
\(-> left\-aligned 4\-digit numbers such as
.Ql "3   " .
.El
.It Fl \-enumerate\-label1 Ar string
For Enumerate mode: string prepended before the line number. Default:
.Ql $\[aq]\[rs]x1b[36m\[aq]
(cyan colour).
.It Fl \-enumerate\-label2 Ar string
For Enumerate mode: string appended after the line number. Default:
.Ql $\[aq]\[rs]x1b[0m \[aq]
(colour reset followed by a space).
.It Fl \-highlight\-begin Ar string
For Highlight mode: marker printed at the start of a marked block. Default: ⭐.
.It Fl \-highlight\-end Ar string
For Highlight mode: marker printed at the end of a marked block. Default: 🛑.
.It Fl \-highlight\-unmarked1 Ar string
For Highlight mode: prefix printed before unmarked text fragments. Default:
.Ql $\[aq]\[rs]x1b[34m\[aq]
(blue colour).
.It Fl \-highlight\-unmarked2 Ar string
For Highlight mode: suffix printed after unmarked text fragments. Default:
.Ql $\[aq]\[rs]x1b[0m\[aq]
(colour reset).
.It Fl \-highlight\-marked1 Ar string
For Highlight mode: prefix printed before marked text fragments. Default:
.Ql $\[aq]\[rs]x1b[31m\[aq]
(red colour).
.It Fl \-highlight\-marked2 Ar string
For Highlight mode: suffix printed after marked text fragments. Default:
.Ql $\[aq]\[rs]x1b[0m\[aq]
(colour reset).
.It Fl \-highlight\-param Ar begin\_label Ar end\_label Ar un\%mar\%ked1\_la\%bel Ar un\%mar\%ked2\_la\%bel Ar mar\%ked1\_la\%bel Ar mar\%ked2\_la\%bel | Fl \-highlight\-params Ar begin\_label Ar end\_label Ar un\%mar\%ked1\_la\%bel Ar un\%mar\%ked2\_la\%bel Ar mar\%ked1\_la\%bel Ar mar\%ked2\_la\%bel
Shortcut to set all 6 highlight parameters at once.
.El
.\" ###### Files ############################################################
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/share/text\-block/example1.txt , example2.txt , insert.txt , numbers.txt
Example input and insertion files installed with System\-Tools.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
Note: the example input files
.Pa example1.txt ,
.Pa example2.txt ,
.Pa insert.txt ,
and
.Pa numbers.txt
referenced below are typically installed under
.Pa /usr/share/text\-block/
or
.Pa /usr/local/share/text\-block/ .
.Ss Cat Mode
.Bl -bullet
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-\-cat
.It
text\-block \-i /etc/system\-info.d/01\-example
.It
text\-block \-i /etc/system\-info.d/01\-example \-C
.El
.Ss Enumerate Mode
.Bl -bullet
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-\-enumerate
.It
figlet \[dq]Test!\[dq] | text\-block \-E
.It
text\-block \-i /etc/system\-info.d/01\-example \-E
.It
text\-block \-i /etc/system\-info.d/01\-example \-\-enumerate \-\-enumerate\-format \[dq]6\[dq] \-\-enumerate\-label1 $\[aq]\[rs]x1b[37m<\[aq] \-\-enumerate\-label2 $\[aq]>\[rs]x1b[0m \[aq]
.El
.Ss Extract Mode
.Bl -bullet
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-\-extract
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-X \-\-include\-tags \-\-full\-tag\-lines
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-\-select 2 4 \-X
.El
.Ss Highlight Mode
.Bl -bullet
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-\-highlight
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-H \-\-exclude\-tags \-\-tags\-only
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-H \-\-include\-tags \-\-tags\-only
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-H \-\-include\-tags \-\-full\-tag\-lines
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-H \-\-exclude\-tags \-\-full\-tag\-lines
.It
text\-block \-i example2.txt \-b \[aq]<MARKER>\[aq] \-H \-\-exclude\-tags \-\-tags\-only
.It
text\-block \-i example2.txt \-b \[aq]<MARKER>\[aq] \-H \-\-include\-tags \-\-tags\-only
.It
text\-block \-i example2.txt \-b \[aq]<MARKER>\[aq] \-H \-\-include\-tags \-\-full\-tag\-lines
.It
text\-block \-i example2.txt \-b \[aq]<MARKER>\[aq] \-H \-\-exclude\-tags \-\-full\-tag\-lines
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-\-highlight \-\-highlight\-params \[dq]☀\[dq] \[dq]🌙\[dq] $\[aq]\[rs]e[32m\[aq] $\[aq]\[rs]e[0m\[aq] $\[aq]\[rs]e[31;5m\[aq] $\[aq]\[rs]e[0m\[aq]
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-\-select 1 3 \-H
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-\-select \-3 \-1 \-H
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-\-select \-5 0 \-H
.El
.Ss Delete Mode
.Bl -bullet
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-\-delete
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-D
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-\-select 2 4 \-D
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-\-select \-4 \-2 \-D
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-s \-7 0 \-D
.El
.Ss Insert Front Mode
.Bl -bullet
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-\-insert\-front insert.txt
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-F insert.txt
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-F insert.txt \-f
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-F insert.txt \-\-min\-actions 1 \-\-max\-actions 1
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-F insert.txt \-m 1 \-M 1
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-F insert.txt \-\-select 4 7
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-F insert.txt \-\-select \-4 \-2
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-F insert.txt \-s 4 0
.El
.Ss Insert Back Mode
.Bl -bullet
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-\-insert\-back insert.txt
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-B insert.txt
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-B insert.txt \-f
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-B insert.txt \-\-min\-actions 1 \-\-max\-actions 1
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-B insert.txt \-m 1 \-M 1
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-B insert.txt \-\-select 4 7
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-B insert.txt \-\-select \-4 \-2
.It
text\-block \-i numbers.txt \-B insert.txt \-s 4 0
.El
.Ss Replace Mode
.Bl -bullet
.It
text\-block \-i example1.txt \-b \[aq]<BEGIN\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-e \[aq]<END\-BLOCK>\[aq] \-\-replace insert.txt
.It
